AUDIO: 'So, you\'ve generated the perfect Google Flow video, but there\'s one problem. [music] That watermark sitting right in the corner, even though you are on a pro plan. Well, I have good news for you. You can remove it in under few minutes for free using one simple tool. Let me'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'show you how. We\'re going to use a free video editor called Shotcut for this. Head over to shotcut.org. The link is in the description below. Click download, then select your'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'operating system. In my [music] case, I\'m choosing Windows. Your download should start automatically within a few seconds. Once it\'s done, go ahead and install the software. Open Shotcut and you\'ll see an'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'interface that looks like this. It\'s actually a full video editor, but for this tutorial, we\'re only using it to remove watermarks. First, create a new project. Select a folder where you want your work saved.'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Type in your project name. Then click start. Next, click open file to import the clip you want to clean up. If you have more'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'than one clip, I\'d recommend importing them all at once, so you can remove every watermark in a single pass. I\'ll go ahead and select three. Click and drag each clip onto your'

[01:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'timeline. Then select the first clip.'

[01:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Click filters. Hit the plus sign and search for spot remover. Select it and you\'ll see a rectangular'

[01:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'box appear on your preview screen. Click and drag that box over the watermark and it will automatically fade it out. Repeat this same process for every [music] clip on your timeline.'

[02:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Once you\'re done, click export then export video.audio.'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
